From 942c1b93efa2433c8c93b3c80d1f556bebff184c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 18:02:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 02/24] fix: locate bundled packages through module resolution

The server looked for its admin UI and its bundled webapps and plugins
only in <appPath>/node_modules. That holds for a global npm install or
a source checkout, but not when dependencies are hoisted beside the
server or kept in a pnpm store, where the admin UI fails with a 500
and no bundled webapps or plugins are found. The Docker images worked
around this by copying packages into the server's own node_modules.

Follow Node's lookup chain from appPath instead, which finds them in
every layout.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Tc38h7UaqvAcPgWkZK3Fcj
