From 01173808319045a6782c73c57cf35eb55a24f80e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 18:12:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 04/24] build(docker): install the server with pnpm

The base images ship pnpm so that the App Store can install plugins
with it. The server images install with pnpm as well, approving only
the canboatjs and serialport build scripts. Workspace tarballs are
pinned with overrides, since pnpm does not reuse a top-level package
to satisfy the server's dependency on it the way npm does.

The copies of @signalk packages and kip into the server's own
node_modules are no longer needed now that the server locates its
bundled packages through module resolution.

Release and image CI build with pnpm; publishing stays with the npm
CLI for OIDC trusted publishing. The npm bundled with Node 24.5 and
later supports it, so the release no longer installs npm globally,
outside any lockfile.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Tc38h7UaqvAcPgWkZK3Fcj
