From f595a1e659a3e33f442ef37504071bd5e0bf21e3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 18:37:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 05/24] feat(appstore): install plugins and webapps with pnpm

Plugins and webapps in the config directory are installed, removed and
restored with pnpm. Dependency build scripts stay disabled and no
lockfile is written, as before. The first pnpm run moves an npm-built
node_modules aside so pnpm can rebuild it from package.json, and puts
it back if pnpm fails; pnpm would otherwise leave npm's hoisted
packages behind.

The server self-update keeps using npm, which owns the global install
it updates. When pnpm is missing the install log says how to add it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Tc38h7UaqvAcPgWkZK3Fcj
