Published base images predate pnpm, so the Dockerfiles install it
themselves until the bases are rebuilt. Release age gating is off for
image builds: pnpm's 24 hour default silently resolved older versions of
freshly released bundled plugins. Only the server tarball, and in core
the admin UI, is added as a direct dependency; the overrides route the
other workspace packages to their tarballs, which keeps the admin UI's
build-only dependencies and their React peers out of the image.
Dockerfile_rel links a pre-pnpm server's node_modules to its siblings so
that older tags still serve the admin UI, and drops the pnpm store and
caches from the single-stage image. pnpm -r pack already packs the root,
so the extra pnpm pack is gone, and the default base is one from the
build matrix.

