From d40a6eeebe05e1a4d55cee183715789c928916e0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 22:41:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 14/24] fix(restore): keep pnpm's links when restoring a backup

pnpm builds node_modules from symbolic links, which the restore wrote
out as regular files, so restored plugins threw at require(). The
extractor reads the central directory, recreates the links, and skips
ones that would point outside the backup. A link target is read only up
to the longest one a file system accepts, whatever size the archive
declares.

Copying into the config directory follows the links it already has, so
a restored link can land where it leads elsewhere than in the backup,
outside included. The copies now finish before plugins are installed,
and each restored link is kept only when it leads to the same entry as
in the backup.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Tc38h7UaqvAcPgWkZK3Fcj
