From 79c5ebf7d9d2d96020fd7dac49ac4a011019a5ca Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 20:04:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 16/24] feat(appstore): install with the pnpm that ships with
 the server

The App Store needed pnpm 11 on PATH and refused to install anything
without it, which users updating from the Admin UI had no way to fix.
The server now depends on pnpm and runs it with its own Node.js, so
plugins install with the pnpm version the server was released with,
without a shell on Windows. The server requires the Node.js that the
bundled pnpm runs on, 22.13 or later, which a test keeps in step, and
an older Node.js is reported instead of failing inside pnpm. The
footer shows the bundled version, and the install docs no longer
install pnpm.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Tc38h7UaqvAcPgWkZK3Fcj
