From e7a540d2ce6829011e8ad7f791da218525a8946d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 20:05:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 17/24] fix(appstore): give the config directory its own pnpm
 store

pnpm picks its store from the project it runs in: on a config directory
mounted from another file system, as in Docker, it used a store in that
directory, while the server probed the store from its own working
directory. The mismatch made every App Store operation rebuild
node_modules, and the store, inside the config directory, went into
settings backups and grew without end.

The App Store now keeps its store and cache in .pnpm-store in the
config directory, so it is always on the file system of node_modules
and hard links work, and asks pnpm for the store path from there.
Settings backups and restores leave the store out. Only the server's
installs use it, so it is pruned after every successful run; replaced
versions leave node_modules at once instead of after a week, so that
pruning frees them. pnpm no longer prints its own update notices into
the install log. Plugin CI installs with the same settings, which a
test keeps in step.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Tc38h7UaqvAcPgWkZK3Fcj
