From efe772e5899fa12ccdaa9bd8f30dcdce575b254b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 20:07:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 20/24] feat: add signalk-pnpm to install plugins from the
 command line

npm no longer works in a config directory that pnpm manages, and a
plain pnpm installs differently from the App Store: with a range it
picks a version older than a day, with a fresh exact version it writes
a pnpm-workspace.yaml, and it uses another store. signalk-pnpm runs
any pnpm command in the config directory the way the App Store does,
with the bundled pnpm, its settings and its store, and with the same
handling of an npm-built node_modules. It finds the config directory
as the server does, starts its package.json as the server would, makes
relative paths absolute from where it was run, and refuses to run as
root in a directory that another user owns.

The server and signalk-pnpm keep their pnpm runs apart with a lock in
the store, which proper-lockfile keeps fresh while it is held, so the
lock of a process that died is taken over within seconds. The holder is
recorded next to the lock, so a holder that is gone from this machine,
as when the server restarts after a crash, gives way at once. A run that
has to wait says so in its log.

The plugin, WASM and Docker docs use it, and the images put the
server's commands on PATH. The server's bin directory is no longer
ignored by git, which hid new commands there, so prettier now checks
it as well.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Tc38h7UaqvAcPgWkZK3Fcj
