Subject: [PATCH 22/24] fix(appstore): never take a package name for a pnpm
 option

npm allows a package name to start with a hyphen, and the App Store
passed the name to pnpm as it was, so an install request for a name
such as --global reached pnpm as an option rather than a package. The
App Store now puts the package after --, where pnpm reads whatever
follows as a package, so names npm allows still install.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
