From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 07:53:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 23/24] fix(appstore): keep packages in use when pruning the
 store

pnpm copies a package with install scripts into node_modules rather than
linking it, so the prune after every App Store operation removed such
packages from the store while they were installed, along with the
metadata cache: each install downloaded them and the metadata again,
and an offline reinstall failed.

The store is now pruned only when a package has left node_modules, as
after a removal or an update, and the store's copies of installed files
that are not linked from node_modules are pinned with a hard link of
their own while it runs. The prune gets a metadata cache of its own to
empty, so the one installs use is kept.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Tc38h7UaqvAcPgWkZK3Fcj
